{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor immediately escalated the combination of chills, increased odor, and wet dressing in a deep burn to same-day in-person evaluation, then maintained safe monitoring through ED, admission/observation, debridement, and discharge transition. All authored responsibility-chain duties were met: systemic and wound red flags, medication/wound-care boundaries, records/follow-up grounding, barrier handling, and patient/family receipt were all made actionable. Multiple high-order points were actively completed, including correcting misunderstandings, verifying ambiguous wet dressings/fever risk without overcalling, discovering and integrating evolving infection/culture/debridement information, and navigating distance/cost/work barriers. Closure was safe and executable after the patient confirmed the wound-center plan, medication restrictions, culture follow-up, and urgent return thresholds.",
